      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the definitions of the geometric mean and harmonic mean. Let the two positive real numbers be \\( a \\) and \\( b \\).\n\n1. **Geometric Mean:**\n   \\[\n   (a \\cdot b)^{1/2} = \\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n   Squaring both sides, we get:\n   \\[\n   a \\cdot b = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Harmonic Mean:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n   \\]\n\nNext, we will use these two equations to solve for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\).\n\nFirst, we express \\( b \\) in terms of \\( a \\) using the geometric mean equation:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{3}{a}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( b \\) into the harmonic mean equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{2a \\left( \\frac{3}{a} \\right)}{a + \\frac{3}{a}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{a + \\frac{3}{a}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nCross-multiply to solve for \\( a \\):\n\\[\n12 = 3a + \\frac{9}{a}\n\\]\n\nMultiply through by \\( a \\) to clear the fraction:\n\\[\n12a = 3a^2 + 9\n\\]\n\nRearrange to form a quadratic equation:\n\\[\n3a^2 - 12a + 9 = 0\n\\]\n\nDivide the entire equation by 3 for simplicity:\n\\[\na^2 - 4a + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nFactor the quadratic equation:\n\\[\n(a - 1)(a - 3) = 0\n\\]\n\nThus, the solutions for \\( a \\) are:\n\\[\na = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = 3\n\\]\n\nUsing \\( b = \\frac{3}{a} \\), we get:\n\nIf \\( a = 1 \\):\n\\[\nb = \\frac{3}{1} = 3\n\\]\n\nIf \\( a = 3 \\):\n\\[\nb = \\frac{3}{3} = 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the two numbers are \\( \\boxed{1, 3} \\).\n\nTo verify, we will plug these values back into the original definitions of the geometric mean and harmonic mean.\n\n1. For \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = 3 \\):\n   - Geometric mean:\n     \\[\n     (1 \\cdot 3)^{1/2} = \\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n   - Harmonic mean:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 3}{1 + 3} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\n     \\]\n\nBoth conditions are satisfied.\n\n2. For \\( a = 3 \\) and \\( b = 1 \\):\n   - Geometric mean:\n     \\[\n     (3 \\cdot 1)^{1/2} = \\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n   - Harmonic mean:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1}{3 + 1} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\n     \\]\n\nBoth conditions are also satisfied.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{1, 3}\\).",
