      "text": "Let the two positive real numbers be $a$ and $b.$  Since the geometric mean is $\\sqrt{3},$ we have\n\\[\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}.\\]Squaring both sides gives $ab = 3.$\n\nLet $h$ be the harmonic mean.  Using this value, we can write\n\\[\\frac{1}{h} = \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b}.\\]Multiplying each term by $ab,$ we get $a + b = ab - 1.$  Since we know $ab = 3,$ we get $a + b = 3 - 1 = 2.$\n\nBy the quadratic formula (see box $10.2.5$), the quadratic $x^2 - (a + b)x + ab = x^2 - 2x + 3 = 0$ has roots $a, b.$  The sum of the roots of $x^2 + bx + c = 0$ is $-b,$ so $a + b = -(-2) = 2.$  Hence, $ab - a - b = 2^2 - 2 = \\boxed{2}.$",
